{"t": 1794118883.008576, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_or_update_file", "args": {"branch": "eng-91", "content": "def deprecation_headers(sunset_date: str) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Return the headers required on a deprecated (v1) endpoint response.\n\n    Per the API guidelines, Deprecation section, a deprecated endpoint must\n    send ``Deprecation: true``, a ``Sunset`` HTTP-date, and a ``Link`` to the\n    migration guide tagged with ``rel=\"deprecation\"``.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        \"Deprecation\": \"true\",\n        \"Sunset\": sunset_date,\n        \"Link\": '<https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"',\n    }\n", "message": "ENG-91: add deprecation headers for v1 endpoints", "owner": "acme", "path": "api/headers.py", "repo": "public-api"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794118886.7341187, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Implements `api.headers.deprecation_headers(sunset_date)` per the API guidelines (Notion, API guidelines > Deprecation):\n\n- `Deprecation: true`\n- `Sunset: <HTTP-date>` (the `sunset_date` argument, passed through as an HTTP-date)\n- `Link: <https://developer.acme.example/migrate>; rel=\"deprecation\"`\n\nCloses ENG-91.", "head": "eng-91", "owner": "acme", "repo": "public-api", "title": "ENG-91: Add deprecation headers to v1 endpoints"}, "ok": true}
